{"ticker":"CAPLIPOINT","symbol":"CAPLIPOINT","instrumentId":3118353,"name":"Caplin Point Lab.","industry":"NSE-Medical-Generic Drugs","about":"Caplin Point Laboratories Ltd., is a dynamic pharmaceutical company known for its strong foothold in Latin America, Francophone Africa, and its growing presence in regulated markets like the USA and EU. Initially focused on manufacturing ointments and creams, the company expanded its product range and production capacity after its 1994 IPO, which was oversubscribed 117 times. Today, Caplin Point is a leading supplier of pharmaceuticals in emerging markets, with over 4,000 product licenses globally. The company is committed to innovation, investing significantly in R&D to develop safe and effective products across various dosage forms.","website":"www.caplinpoint.net","location":"INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:11:27.346Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":2084.6,"changePct":-0.03356831151394393,"week52High":2867.4,"week52Low":1504.8},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹15,845 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹2,383 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"22,043,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"202"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"6,024,642"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.38%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"4.51"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"0.8"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.06"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.88"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"20%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"23"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"14–38"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"18.3%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"68.84"},{"label":"Volume","value":"160,636"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"163,570"},{"label":"Master score","value":"56"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"76"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"60"},{"label":"Group rank","value":"31"},{"label":"Acc/Dis rating","value":"E"}],"earningsAnnual":{"headers":["Ye